<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">trip</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">trip</ansi> command sweeps your opponent's legs out from under them,
knocking them to the ground. It deals modest damage and is primarily
a tactical move rather than a finisher.

<ansi fg="yellow">Requirements:</ansi>

  - Must be in active combat
  - Cannot be used if special move cooldown is active

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">trip</ansi>
  Attempt to trip your current combat target

<ansi fg="yellow">Mechanics:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="stat">Damage:</ansi> Light — the goal is the floor, not the hit.
  <ansi fg="stat">Knockdown Chance:</ansi> The most reliable knockdown of the three
    special moves, resolved against the defender's Dexterity and
    combat skill.
  <ansi fg="stat">Cooldown:</ansi> Shared with bash and kick.
  <ansi fg="stat">Skill:</ansi> Progresses Unarmed Combat

Trip's high knockdown rate makes it excellent for setting up your
allies' attacks. If successful, your target becomes <ansi fg="red">prone</ansi>
for a short time. See <ansi fg="command">help prone</ansi> for details.

<ansi fg="yellow">See Also:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">help bash</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help kick</ansi>,
